        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The Labrador is a variety of domestic dog. Labradors have fur that can be brown, black or yellow.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 20
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In Labradors, <i>TYRP1</i> is one gene that codes for fur colour. This gene has two alleles, <b>B</b> and <b>b</b>.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 20
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "The dominant allele, <b>B</b>, codes for the enzyme tyrosinase that functions in the pathway to produce melanin, leading to black fur.",
              "The production of melanin in Labradors is very similar to the production of melanin in humans.",
              "The recessive allele, <b>b</b>, codes for an enzyme that results in the production of a brown form of melanin, leading to brown fur."
            ],
            "source": {
              "qp": 20
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Outline how melanin may be produced in Labradors to produce black fur.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "16.2(6)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 2,
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>two</i></b><i> from: </i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "tyrosine converted to, DOPA / dopaquinone <b>; </b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "dopaquinone converted to melanin <b>; </b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "<i>ref. to</i> melanocytes <b>; </b>"
            }
          ],
          "source": {
            "ms": 19
          }
        },
        "er": [
          "er.q7.a"
        ],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "The pathway begins with an amino acid substrate and ends with a pigment product. Use the enzyme to connect those chemical conversions rather than giving only the allele combination responsible for the colour.",
              "refs": [
                "ms:a#1",
                "ms:a#2",
                "ms:a#3",
                "syllabus:16.2(6)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Follow tyrosine through its intermediates.",
            "Identify the pigment formed and the cell type involved."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": []
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 21
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Another gene, <i>MC1R</i>, interacts with <i>TYRP1</i>.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 21
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<i>MC1R</i> has two alleles, <b>E</b> and <b>e</b>.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 21
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "The dominant allele, <b>E</b>, allows the alleles of <i>TYRP1</i> to be expressed.",
              "The recessive allele, <b>e</b>, prevents the alleles of <i>TYRP1</i> from being expressed.",
              "When no form of melanin is produced the Labrador will have yellow fur."
            ],
            "source": {
              "qp": 21
            }
          }
        ],
